{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551392-loophole-for-lost-eggs-who-take-the-razor","id":1551392,"title":"Loophole for Lost Eggs who take the razor?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-01T11:52:58-07:00","id":1551392,"title":"Loophole for Lost Eggs who take the razor?","content":"So I am new to the setting and was reading the Realm book and the dragonblooded book and I noticed what might be a loophole. Taking the razor as a lost egg is supposed to be for life, that's part of the appeal of the coin, you only give fifty years compared to a lifetime of service.<br /> <br /> But a monk can leave the order whenever they want. They can decide they don't want to be a monk anymore, and the order gives them a month to think it over. Then, the order pretends the former monk was never a monk.<br /> <br /> Couldn't a lost egg take the razor, take their oaths, and then quit whenever they feel like and use their knowledge, education, and exaltation to gain political power among patricians or minor cadet houses?<br /> <br /> Or would they just be told that no, they don't get that option, or told to get to the legion, or quietly eliminated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-01T20:41:25-07:00","id":1551405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551392-loophole-for-lost-eggs-who-take-the-razor#post1551392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I am new to the setting and was reading the Realm book and the dragonblooded book and I noticed what might be a loophole. Taking the razor as a lost egg is supposed to be for life, that's part of the appeal of the coin, you only give fifty years compared to a lifetime of service.<br /> <br /> But a monk can leave the order whenever they want. They can decide they don't want to be a monk anymore, and the order gives them a month to think it over. Then, the order pretends the former monk was never a monk.<br /> <br /> Couldn't a lost egg take the razor, take their oaths, and then quit whenever they feel like and use their knowledge, education, and exaltation to gain political power among patricians or minor cadet houses?<br /> <br /> Or would they just be told that no, they don't get that option, or told to get to the legion, or quietly eliminated?</div> </div> </div> </div>They address right at the end of discussing taking the Razor in <b>What Fire Has Wrought</b>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Outcaste monks ejected from the order were traditionally remanded to the Empress for punishment or the assignment of alternative duties to the throne. </div> </div> </div>Basically you don't just get to go out and join the patriciate. You'll be assigned some task that the Empress would have found useful for you that either makes an exmaple out of you for the Order's sake, or is useful for her own sake. You get the knowledge, education, and whatnot. But the Empress more or less got a leash on you from then out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T04:57:47-07:00","id":1551412,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s so obvious it seems more like a giant hole in the wall than a loophole, but if it\u2019s really that easy to leave the Order, then yes, a Lost Egg who takes the razor could get out of it that way and use their newfound knowledge, education and exaltation to gain power in Dragon-Blooded society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T07:41:51-07:00","id":1551419,"title":"","content":"I think it doesn't need to be explicitly forbidden so much as something that will leave one extremely ostracised. Like, Dynasts who renounce their vows aren't exactly popular as it is.<br /> <br /> How exactly are you going to gain political power in Dragon-Blooded society among people who will not give you the time of day? What patricians will want to take the hit to their reputation that associating with you will entail?<br /> <br /> Mind, looking back at the information, it says that if an Outcaste is ejected from the order, they're remanded to the Empress for punishment or assignment to alternative duties. Given that the premise of the razor and the coin is that a Lost Egg is essentially an adopted child of the Empress and bound to directly obey her, I suppose the idea of personally renouncing the order is somewhere between outright forbidden without her dispensation and something that would have gotten you picked up by her agents and put to other purposes.<br /> <br /> Like, it's not going to have loopholes because it's not a function of some legislative ephemera. Non-dynastic Dragon-Blooded are obligated to become monks or soldiers by the decree of an autocrat. Attempting to not play along with that is going to go the usual way.<br /> <br /> The Time of Tumult, at least, might have an Outcaste monk try their hand at leaving the order under the basis that its own rules technically permit that and they may have less to fear from imperial authorities. But again, they're going to be doing something that already carries a bit of stigma while having no other basis for social standing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-04T21:22:21-07:00","id":1551469,"title":"","content":"IIRC, back in the early days of 1e the original developer commented that it was possible to join the Order, learn Immaculate Martial Arts, and leave, but [paraphrased from memory] &quot;Good luck being a defrocked monk in a highly religious society.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-06T00:59:19-07:00","id":1551496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551392-loophole-for-lost-eggs-who-take-the-razor?p=1551469#post1551469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, back in the early days of 1e the original developer commented that it was possible to join the Order, learn Immaculate Martial Arts, and leave, but [paraphrased from memory] &quot;Good luck being a defrocked monk in a highly religious society.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You're <i>so</i> marrying a patrician.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's in the 1e DB errata, in case anyone wants to look for it. The same doc that graced us with the grand goremaul aka thousand measure staff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-06T09:21:46-07:00","id":1551500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551392-loophole-for-lost-eggs-who-take-the-razor?p=1551496#post1551496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;You're <i>so</i> marrying a patrician.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly a step down if you went from slave or peasant to outcaste tbh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-06T19:05:47-07:00","id":1551509,"title":"","content":"The original errata and context was for just the DB book, which by default gave cahrgen for Dynasts only. You're likely just not getting married at all if you were an outcaste. Or as noted, assigned to something menial by the Empress (less the case these days, mind).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-07T06:10:11-07:00","id":1551514,"title":"","content":"Given that the options for outcastes are to either join up for a lengthy term of service to a duty that is likely to lead to their deaths or become celibate for life, I don't think preserving their bloodlines is a high priority.<br /> <br /> In which case, why should one that has disgraced themselves by forsaking their holy vows be allowed to marry at all? That's not even something that needs to come from the top down, just a matter of the difficulty of finding a judge who is willing to risk the political fallout of signing off on it.<br /> <br /> What patrician even wants that heat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-08T08:52:21-07:00","id":1551526,"title":"","content":"From the patrician house's perspective the idea that they turned their back of a lifetime commitment actually represents the best case scenario, it's also very plausible that their departure from the Immaculate Order was not entirely willing and <i>who knows</i> what skeletons might be in their closet or what behaviour they think they'll be able to repeat without a bunch of other Exalts around to stop them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-22T11:32:37-07:00","id":1551821,"title":"","content":"Officially, the answer is &quot;The Scarlet Empress finds some unpleasant duty for them, as an example to others.&quot; I think the details would probably depend on A) how long they were in the Order, and B) why they left. A novice who was forcibly expelled under a cloud of scandal could end up &quot;counting penguins in Fajad&quot;. One who simply decided the monastic life wasn't for them but still wants to join the Legions would be hazed even more mercilessly than usual at Pesiap's Stair, but if they survived would be just another officer. And a monk who served faithfully for two centuries before falling in love and wanting to marry might not be punished at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26077,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26077-chaotic-nipple","user":"Chaotic-nipple","date":". 06-28-2025, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26077-chaotic-nipple","name":"Chaotic-nipple","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T03:42:48-07:00","id":1552097,"title":"","content":"I imagine at least one Magistrate found themselves in the position this way. It's like Tepet Elena was made one for her insubordination in staying behind to protect wounded soldiers, but the Empress made her true real feelings about that abundantly clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}